    {
      "label": "Consider if lien_initiator needs to be a Pubkey or if it could be a simple Enum (e.g., LienSource::Client, LienSource::Freelancer, LienSource::None). This saves space (1 byte vs 32 bytes) and makes logic checks explicit, preventing a scenario where a random third party is somehow written to this field.",
      "entryType": 1,
      "author": "macbook",
      "details": {
        "severity": "",
        "difficulty": "",
        "type": "",
        "description": "another case,  Zero-Initialization Risks\n\nObservation: When a dispute is resolved, does lien_initiator get cleared (zeroed out)?\nRisk: If the logic checks if lien_initiator != Pubkey::default(), ensure that your \"resolve\" instruction properly resets this field. Otherwise, a job might get stuck in a \"pseudo-dispute\" state if the status changes but the initiator field remains dirty",
        "exploit": "",
        "recommendation": "Short term, \nLong term, \n"
